## Voice (for any agent that produces customer-facing or official-communication content in this repo)

Voice is pack-driven. The active pack's voice tier (`resolve_pack_field voice.default_tier`; neutral default: `internal`) determines the default style, and a pack may supply a voice corpus (`resolve_pack_field voice.corpus`; none by default) plus a critic that checks customer-facing output before it lands. If this repo produces customer-bound or official-communication output, agents that generate it declare a non-internal voice tier and follow whatever guidelines the active pack defines.

Internal dev agents (CodeReviewer, TestRunner, planning, etc.) declare `voice: internal` and use the direct "builder talking to builder" style.

When in doubt: internal voice is the default. Use a customer-facing tier only for genuinely customer-bound content.
